		["helpDebug"] = "print(...) writes to Output. addon and editor refer to LuaWorkbench. Errors remain in Output; execution status appears separately. Copy output selects the output for Ctrl+C. The output line limit is configurable; a 64,000-character cap also applies. Format code runs only when requested. Options control fonts, indentation, bracket completion, LF/CRLF and the minimap button. After manually clearing output, Undo is available for 10 seconds. Output added afterward is kept when restoring; the configured output limit still applies.",
		["helpDump"] = "dump(...) writes each argument separately to Output, preserving nil values between arguments and at the end. dump({...}) instead dumps one table. Example: dump(\"value\", nil, false). DevTools_Dump(value, startKey) keeps its original signature; its optional second argument names the dumped value. This applies to manual runs, automatic runs, helper modules and the debug terminal. These functions are local to the script environment; global functions remain unchanged. Multiple arguments are labelled arg[1], arg[2], etc.; a single argument stays unnumbered. Table contents remain grouped under their argument label. Use dump(...) to retain nil arguments: a table created with {...} does not retain the full argument count. Large dumps expand the retained output buffer until it is cleared. The 30-entry table limit does not apply; Blizzard depth and string limits still apply.",
		["helpEditing"] = "With focus in the code or search fields: Ctrl+Enter runs, Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+F searches this code, Ctrl+Shift+F searches all script names and code. F5 runs while the editor has focus or the pointer is over it; disable it in Options. In code: Tab inserts spaces, Shift+Tab removes leading indentation. In search: Enter / Shift+Enter selects the next / previous match; Escape closes code search. While renaming: Enter confirms, Escape cancels. Right-click editable code to format all code or insert a saved text snippet or helper import at the current cursor. Definition navigation is available in the main editor only. Shift+Alt+F formats the focused code editor, including the text-snippet editor. In the main code editor: Ctrl+Space opens completion, Up/Down selects, Enter / Tab inserts and Esc closes it. API parameter hints mark the current argument. Alt+Up/Down moves the current line; Alt+Shift+Up/Down duplicates it. Without a selection, Ctrl+C/X copies/cuts the line; Ctrl+V inserts copied lines above the current line. Saved line endings follow Options. (macOS: ⌘C / ⌘X / ⌘V). Mac: Ctrl+Backspace deletes one character, Option+Backspace deletes the previous word, and Cmd+Backspace deletes to the start of the line. Mac: Option+Left/Right moves by word; Cmd+Left/Right moves to line start/end. Add Shift to extend the selection. Cmd+Up/Down moves to the start/end of the code; add Shift to select.",
